    "summary": "Good Lovin', wild Hard‑To‑Handle run, but tape is muddy",
    "blurb": "The set features a fiery Hard To Handle → China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider segue and two punchy Good Lovin' renditions bookending the show. Turn On Your Lovelight provides a bright jam while Pigpen’s organ adds color. The audience recording is extremely noisy, making much of the performance hard to hear.",
    "review": "On May 3, 1970 the Grateful Dead took the stage at Foss Hill, Wesleyan University for a free concert that blended acoustic openings, a New Riders set (highlighted by Jerry’s pedal‑steel) and a brief but spirited Dead main set. The band launched into a hard‑driving “Hard To Handle” that segued into a classic “China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider” pairing, followed later by two energetic versions of “Good Lovin'”. A bright “Turn On Your Lovelight” jam and Pigpen’s organ work added texture, even as the crowd’s drunken din dominates the tape. Unfortunately, all available recordings are audience‑mic captures riddled with heavy crowd noise and low fidelity, so many moments are lost in the mix. Listeners willing to brave the rough sound will be rewarded by the occasional clear bursts of jamming and historic context of a protest‑era campus show.",
